NAME      jitArgBake -- an own-function JIT callee reads `argument` at the
          emit-time BAKED address, not the run-time bound slot.

WHAT      Where the JIT gives a callee its own function instead of inlining it,
          the callee's `argument` read is a load from an address baked when the
          body was compiled. The run-time bind (jitBindArgRT) writes somewhere
          else, so the emitted body reads whatever was bound at COMPILE time --
          and prints an address where the interpreter prints 7. Silent: degrade
          count 0, exit 0. Inlined callees are CORRECT; this is only the
          own-function road.

WHERE     jitEmitters.rtn -- jitBindArgRT binds at run time; jitEmitBareRead
          and jitSeedField bake at emit time. The two never meet.

WHY NOW   B landed 2026-09-05 and fixed the inlined road on both engines. This
          is what B did not reach. PRE-EXISTING, not caused by B -- the same
          read answered 0 before B.

WHAT YOU JUST RAN. Two blocks, same action, same input, two engines. The
interpreted block is the oracle and prints 7 twice. The jitted block prints an
address twice. The LOCAL column agrees on both engines, which is what says the
defect is the argument channel and not the frame.

THE DISCRIMINATOR IS ONE LINE IN THE RUN: `callee jabA built as jit_jabA`
means own-function, and therefore in scope. Its absence means the callee
inlined and is already correct -- minionWork/probeArgJit is that case and reads
8 / 22 / oracle 14 at degrade 0.

NEXT: BEST GUESS -- feed a slot, stop baking.

Tony's words, 2026-09-05. jitBindArgRT already runs at the right moment and
already knows the passed field; what it does not do is put that field where the
emitted body will look. The emitter's side is the mirror -- jitEmitBareRead and
jitSeedField compute a home address from the argument node at emit time, which
for an own-function callee is a fact that has not happened yet.

⚠ IT IS A CANDIDATE, NOT A RULING, and one measurement promotes or kills it:
does the own-function road have a frame slot for the argument at all, or only
the baked home? The frame prologue walks (isLocal || isArgument) over the
action's field list, so if the argument reaches the prologue it already has an
alloca and the fix is to make jitBindArgRT store into it. If it does not, the
slot has to be created first and the stroke is larger.

WHAT WOULD KILL IT: if one emitted function is shared across call sites with
different arguments, a slot is not enough and the argument has to become a real
function parameter. That is a much larger shape. Find out which one this is
BEFORE building either.

